1
00:01:56,439 --> 00:01:57,200
What brings you here?

2
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:59,519
Tech found Lin Kanshan's entry records.

3
00:01:59,879 --> 00:02:01,400
But he didn't go back to Minzhong.

4
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,480
He went to Guangdong instead.

5
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:04,120
Stayed for a bit, then left.

6
00:02:04,120 --> 00:02:05,480
He probably headed over to Europe.

7
00:02:06,599 --> 00:02:08,240
Doesn't sound like anything urgent.

8
00:02:08,719 --> 00:02:09,960
I thought there was a new mission

9
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,159
and they were tying you to me again.

10
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,680
Did you have to come all this way to tell me?

11
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:15,800
I was just passing by

12
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:17,960
and thought I might score a late-night bite.

13
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:23,759
Why was your phone off when I called?

14
00:02:24,240 --> 00:02:24,800
Battery died.

15
00:02:34,319 --> 00:02:36,080
I can tell you rarely cook at home.

16
00:02:36,560 --> 00:02:39,439
You can't just drink with canned food.

17
00:02:39,919 --> 00:02:41,319
I never touch a drop of alcohol at home.

18
00:02:41,520 --> 00:02:43,000
I never drink when I'm alone.

19
00:02:43,199 --> 00:02:45,080
Then who drank all this wine?

20
00:02:45,400 --> 00:02:47,319
Can't I use it as cooking wine?

21
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,280
Why do you have so many questions?

22
00:02:49,759 --> 00:02:51,479
Were you born with this bad habit?

23
00:02:53,919 --> 00:02:54,879
When I was a kid,

24
00:02:55,319 --> 00:02:56,199
I didn't like to talk.

25
00:02:56,479 --> 00:02:57,960
My dad thought I was useless that way.

26
00:02:58,199 --> 00:02:58,960
He said it so much

27
00:02:58,960 --> 00:03:00,039
that I heard it constantly.

28
00:03:00,159 --> 00:03:01,280
Hearing it so much made me wonder,

29
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,960
shouldn't I talk more?

30
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:05,680
As if being quiet were a character flaw.

31
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:07,159
But I didn't know what to say,

32
00:03:07,759 --> 00:03:09,479
so I just asked about whatever I saw.

33
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:12,360
Over time, it became a habit.

34
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:15,080
Have you always been this obedient?

35
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:16,919
Growing up, did you ever wonder

36
00:03:16,919 --> 00:03:18,280
if what other people said was wrong?

37
00:03:19,159 --> 00:03:20,360
Never before.

38
00:03:21,159 --> 00:03:22,080
But after meeting you,

39
00:03:22,680 --> 00:03:23,479
it's the first time I've felt that way.

40
00:03:24,879 --> 00:03:26,120
Are you praising me or insulting me?

41
00:03:27,400 --> 00:03:30,159
Many people and things change.

42
00:03:30,560 --> 00:03:32,120
We deal with human beings.

43
00:03:32,120 --> 00:03:33,240
People change.

44
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,479
One day to the next,

45
00:03:34,680 --> 00:03:36,280
one second to the next,

46
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:37,919
their thoughts might completely change.

47
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,800
A good person in the first half of life

48
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:41,560
might turn bad in old age.

49
00:03:41,560 --> 00:03:42,879
A bad person in the first half of life

50
00:03:43,319 --> 00:03:45,759
might turn good in old age.

51
00:03:46,479 --> 00:03:47,599
That's what you say.

52
00:03:50,360 --> 00:03:51,400
What do you think makes a good person?

53
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:54,280
Looking in the mirror at night

54
00:03:54,280 --> 00:03:55,960
without fear or guilt—

55
00:03:56,159 --> 00:03:57,159
that's a good person.

56
00:03:57,479 --> 00:03:58,080
Wrong.

57
00:03:58,800 --> 00:04:00,280
That's your definition of a good person.

58
00:04:00,280 --> 00:04:02,400
The worst people feel less guilty than you.

59
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:04,159
Because nobody thinks they're evil.

60
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,639
Even when they do awful things,

61
00:04:05,639 --> 00:04:07,199
they come up with countless excuses.

62
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,680
They even feel wronged themselves.

63
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,080
I don't see it that way.

64
00:04:12,240 --> 00:04:13,000
The way I see it,

65
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,120
everyone has a ledger in their heart.

66
00:04:15,879 --> 00:04:17,040
Good and bad are separated by a line.

67
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:18,279
Some people are on this side,

68
00:04:18,279 --> 00:04:19,240
some are on that side,

69
00:04:19,639 --> 00:04:20,920
and some are in the middle.

70
00:04:23,199 --> 00:04:24,199
Maybe if you pull them,

71
00:04:24,480 --> 00:04:25,480
they'll cross over.

72
00:04:30,079 --> 00:04:31,040
Quite the philosopher, aren't you?

73
00:04:31,319 --> 00:04:33,879
I rarely see you drink this much.

74
00:04:37,680 --> 00:04:38,279
What is it?

75
00:04:38,759 --> 00:04:40,439
Do you have something on your mind

76
00:04:40,560 --> 00:04:42,480
you can only say with liquid courage?

77
00:04:46,759 --> 00:04:48,120
Lin Kanshan has entered the country again.

78
00:04:49,680 --> 00:04:51,480
Who knows when he'll be back?

79
00:04:51,800 --> 00:04:53,839
When he returns, I'll have to play along.

80
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,519
Luckily, today is still relaxing,

81
00:04:55,839 --> 00:04:57,040
and I can chat with you.

82
00:04:57,879 --> 00:04:58,759
Did we have to talk tonight?

83
00:04:58,759 --> 00:04:59,600
Couldn't we talk tomorrow?

84
00:05:00,279 --> 00:05:01,759
Tomorrow brings tomorrow's worries.

85
00:05:02,079 --> 00:05:03,160
You have your cases,

86
00:05:03,439 --> 00:05:04,639
and I have targets to watch.

87
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,920
Lin Kanshan isn't my only target.

88
00:05:06,920 --> 00:05:08,160
You're busy with plenty of cases, too.

89
00:05:08,439 --> 00:05:10,959
By then, I might not get to drink with you.

90
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:15,319
The night is long.

91
00:05:15,959 --> 00:05:17,560
You could talk to Jinlan.

92
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,240
The night is too long.

93
00:05:21,879 --> 00:05:23,439
Some stories, if told,

94
00:05:23,439 --> 00:05:24,240
might scare her.

95
00:05:26,759 --> 00:05:27,600
What stories?

96
00:05:32,800 --> 00:05:33,920
In 1983.

97
00:05:34,399 --> 00:05:36,240
I was ten during the Strike Hard Campaign.

98
00:05:36,240 --> 00:05:37,480
On the first day of summer break,

99
00:05:37,839 --> 00:05:39,360
my cousin dragged me along,

100
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,879
saying he'd show me the world.

101
00:05:41,959 --> 00:05:44,480
He took me to our county's firing range.

102
00:05:45,560 --> 00:05:47,319
From a distance, I saw

103
00:05:47,639 --> 00:05:49,279
a row of condemned prisoners

104
00:05:49,480 --> 00:05:50,639
kneeling on the loess slope.

105
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:52,519
I ran up the hillside.

106
00:05:53,040 --> 00:05:54,519
Just as I reached the crest,

107
00:05:55,879 --> 00:05:56,879
the shots rang out.

108
00:05:57,519 --> 00:05:58,600
One after another.

109
00:05:59,480 --> 00:06:00,680
And then another.

110
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:03,600
That was the first time I heard gunfire.

111
00:06:05,079 --> 00:06:06,079
Deafening.

112
00:06:08,199 --> 00:06:09,560
I'll never forget it as long as I live.

113
00:06:15,879 --> 00:06:19,000
The last one kneeling was a man.

114
00:06:19,680 --> 00:06:21,879
I remember a sign hanging around his neck.

115
00:06:22,199 --> 00:06:23,680
Five characters were written on it:

116
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,279
"Kuomintang Spy."

117
00:06:28,560 --> 00:06:29,759
He was the only one left.

118
00:06:30,319 --> 00:06:32,560
Everyone waited for the final gunshot.

119
00:06:33,199 --> 00:06:34,560
But for some reason,

120
00:06:35,399 --> 00:06:37,560
the young armed officer was slow.

121
00:06:38,399 --> 00:06:39,839
Probably out of nerves.

122
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:43,160
He was anxious, the onlookers were too,

123
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:46,120
and so was the man waiting to be shot.

124
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,079
The spy suddenly turned around,

125
00:06:48,360 --> 00:06:48,920
and asked,

126
00:06:49,399 --> 00:06:50,680
"Why haven't you shot me yet?"

127
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,480
The more he urged him,

128
00:06:52,879 --> 00:06:54,560
the more flustered the young officer got.

129
00:06:54,879 --> 00:06:56,399
The target was the back of his head,

130
00:06:56,839 --> 00:06:58,560
but almost fired straight into his face.

131
00:07:00,680 --> 00:07:02,959
After getting yelled at,

132
00:07:02,959 --> 00:07:04,399
the man turned his head back.

133
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,759
Not long after turning back, though,

134
00:07:06,959 --> 00:07:08,040
he tried to turn around again,

135
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:09,120
wanting to rush him once more.

136
00:07:09,839 --> 00:07:11,160
Before the words left his mouth,

137
00:07:13,040 --> 00:07:13,720
the gun went off.

138
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:16,160
I thought I was just going for the show,

139
00:07:16,920 --> 00:07:17,680
but I ended up seeing

140
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:19,519
something I'll never forget in my life.

141
00:07:22,319 --> 00:07:23,160
Even now,

142
00:07:23,439 --> 00:07:25,000
I still have frequent nightmares.

143
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,240
You were so far away from him.

144
00:07:33,240 --> 00:07:34,519
Could you really hear what they said?

145
00:07:35,079 --> 00:07:37,920
The young officer who fired was my uncle.

146
00:07:38,319 --> 00:07:39,240
He told me about it.

147
00:07:39,879 --> 00:07:41,519
Am I talking too much today?

148
00:07:43,160 --> 00:07:44,439
Truth is, I'm just a coward.

149
00:07:44,800 --> 00:07:45,839
I can't take it,

150
00:07:46,959 --> 00:07:48,839
and I never want to see that again.

151
00:07:54,959 --> 00:07:55,839
A lot of things

152
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:59,399
aren't up to you whether you see them.

153
00:08:01,079 --> 00:08:01,639
Unless...

154
00:08:02,800 --> 00:08:04,040
unless you quit State Security.

155
00:08:58,039 --> 00:08:59,039
Oh, my god!

156
00:09:00,600 --> 00:09:01,960
You hit me, man!

157
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,639
Are you okay? Are you all right?

158
00:09:03,639 --> 00:09:05,120
No, I'm not! I'm not okay!

159
00:09:05,720 --> 00:09:07,480
Listen, I'm calling the police.

160
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,759
No, don't! Don't!

161
00:09:08,759 --> 00:09:09,679
Sorry. I'm really sorry.

162
00:09:09,799 --> 00:09:11,440
You should have stopped!

163
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:12,919
I'm sorry.

164
00:09:13,200 --> 00:09:14,039
I'm so sorry.

165
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:15,159
I'm badly hurt!

166
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:16,360
I didn't mean to, okay?

167
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:17,840
My shoulder! God!

168
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:19,799
Let's wait for the police.

169
00:09:19,799 --> 00:09:20,279
No, no, no!

170
00:09:20,279 --> 00:09:21,480
Can't you see how bad you hit me?

171
00:09:22,519 --> 00:09:23,720
Get in the car. I'll handle this.

172
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:25,240
Roll up the window. Stay inside.

173
00:09:29,559 --> 00:09:30,360
Stop! Stop!

174
00:09:30,360 --> 00:09:32,200
This is murder!

175
00:09:33,039 --> 00:09:34,600
No, no!

176
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:37,799
It hurts so bad! I can't take it!

177
00:09:38,320 --> 00:09:39,399
I'm hurt too badly!

178
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:57,000
How much is it?

179
00:09:57,279 --> 00:09:58,639
Bro, I'll pay you double.

180
00:09:58,919 --> 00:09:59,600
Don't worry about it.

181
00:09:59,799 --> 00:10:00,679
We're all Chinese.

182
00:10:00,919 --> 00:10:02,039
Happy to help when I can.

183
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:02,799
Forget about money.

184
00:10:03,559 --> 00:10:04,720
I was terrified he'd call the cops.

185
00:10:04,919 --> 00:10:05,639
You know, bro?

186
00:10:05,679 --> 00:10:07,320
Is your driver's license expired?

187
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:09,960
I only have my Chinese driver's license.

188
00:10:10,919 --> 00:10:12,279
And my student visa is about to expire.

189
00:10:12,279 --> 00:10:14,240
If he called the cops, I'd be in big trouble.

190
00:10:15,200 --> 00:10:16,879
They don't recognize Chinese licenses here.

191
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:19,360
Don't worry, I sorted it all out for you.

192
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,840
Don't drive without a license next time.

193
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Today,

194
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:23,360
I really can't thank you enough, bro.

195
00:10:23,360 --> 00:10:26,360
It's nothing. Just buy me a meal sometime.

196
00:10:26,639 --> 00:10:27,519
Well, no time like the present.

197
00:10:27,919 --> 00:10:29,039
How about today, bro?

198
00:10:29,120 --> 00:10:30,480
Come on, dinner's on me.

199
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:31,440
I just told you,

200
00:10:31,639 --> 00:10:32,919
don't drive without a license.

201
00:10:32,919 --> 00:10:33,480
I'll drive.

202
00:10:33,639 --> 00:10:34,240
Okay.

203
00:10:46,759 --> 00:10:47,399
Bro,

204
00:10:47,919 --> 00:10:49,240
you're heading back so soon?

205
00:10:50,679 --> 00:10:52,240
Heading to the mainland or Taiwan, China?

206
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,200
I've always traveled back and forth.

207
00:10:54,559 --> 00:10:55,519
Making a living,

208
00:10:56,159 --> 00:10:57,840
you go wherever the money is, right?

209
00:10:58,879 --> 00:10:59,840
Next time we meet,

210
00:11:00,519 --> 00:11:02,960
it'll probably be in Minzhong or Xiamen.

211
00:11:07,759 --> 00:11:08,679
It's good to go back, though.

212
00:11:08,679 --> 00:11:09,399
At least back there, I won't have to eat

213
00:11:09,399 --> 00:11:10,919
this bland Western food anymore.

214
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:11,960
Will you come back?

215
00:11:12,120 --> 00:11:12,639
Yeah.

216
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,399
But definitely not as often.

217
00:11:15,360 --> 00:11:17,960
Have you seen the mainland's rapid growth?

218
00:11:18,320 --> 00:11:19,840
It's taken off like a rocket.

219
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:21,240
If I don't hustle,

220
00:11:21,799 --> 00:11:22,919
even if I can't catch the rocket,

221
00:11:23,279 --> 00:11:24,759
smelling the exhaust is good enough.

222
00:11:29,240 --> 00:11:32,559
Your mom is an expert in education,

223
00:11:32,799 --> 00:11:34,159
and your family understands policy.

224
00:11:34,759 --> 00:11:37,159
She provides the tips, I do the legwork.

225
00:11:37,399 --> 00:11:38,679
Set up an introduction for us.

226
00:11:38,679 --> 00:11:39,799
We can make a fortune together.

227
00:11:41,679 --> 00:11:42,720
What do you mean?

228
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,039
Policies,

229
00:11:46,480 --> 00:11:47,559
land,

230
00:11:48,039 --> 00:11:49,039
pricing.

231
00:11:49,480 --> 00:11:51,960
Just like this plate of seafood rice—

232
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:54,480
will the government eat it or toss it?

233
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:56,159
How much are they willing to spend?

234
00:11:56,159 --> 00:11:57,960
For how long, and how will they eat it?

235
00:11:58,600 --> 00:11:59,840
Once we know what's going on,

236
00:11:59,840 --> 00:12:01,120
we'll have the upper hand.

237
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:02,679
It's just like trading stocks.

238
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:04,840
Only when you know the inside scoop

239
00:12:04,840 --> 00:12:06,320
can you buy at the bottom.

240
00:12:08,799 --> 00:12:11,200
Did I not make myself clear?

241
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:17,879
Just introduce me to your relatives

242
00:12:18,639 --> 00:12:19,639
who work in the government.

243
00:12:19,879 --> 00:12:20,919
I'll talk to them.

244
00:12:21,159 --> 00:12:22,200
We'll make a fortune together.

245
00:12:25,919 --> 00:12:27,960
The boss told me to check on you guys.

246
00:12:27,960 --> 00:12:29,320
He's closing up.

247
00:12:30,360 --> 00:12:31,080
But it's fine.

248
00:12:31,399 --> 00:12:32,559
If you don't want to leave, just stay.

249
00:12:32,559 --> 00:12:33,759
He can't do anything about it.

250
00:12:36,440 --> 00:12:37,240
Let's head out.

251
00:12:37,720 --> 00:12:38,600
Don't let them rush us.

252
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:47,000
What I mean is,

253
00:12:47,320 --> 00:12:49,559
let's find a place open all night

254
00:12:49,559 --> 00:12:50,320
and keep drinking,

255
00:12:50,879 --> 00:12:51,679
drink our fill.

256
00:13:14,240 --> 00:13:15,639
I only found out today

257
00:13:16,480 --> 00:13:17,159
that you

258
00:13:19,159 --> 00:13:20,440
are his landlord.

259
00:13:22,399 --> 00:13:24,240
A subletter, actually.

260
00:13:25,399 --> 00:13:26,919
I'm renting this place, too.

261
00:13:27,799 --> 00:13:28,960
Do you have any rooms available?

262
00:13:29,679 --> 00:13:30,919
I want to move in, too.

263
00:13:36,960 --> 00:13:38,440
Well, I'll have to think about it.

264
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:39,200
Think about it?

265
00:13:40,480 --> 00:13:41,039
No need to think.

266
00:13:41,159 --> 00:13:41,639
Come on.

267
00:13:56,279 --> 00:13:58,080
Stop drinking.

268
00:13:58,440 --> 00:13:59,720
You'll get drunk if you keep going.

269
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:01,000
No, it's not that.

270
00:14:01,240 --> 00:14:03,759
My cigarettes... I'm all out.

271
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:05,080
Do you have any here?

272
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:06,919
I saw some just now.

273
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:08,600
Look for them yourself.

274
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:35,879
What's wrong?

275
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,799
This is Lin Kanshan's.

276
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,360
What about Lin Kanshan's?

277
00:14:43,200 --> 00:14:44,039
I can't smoke this.

278
00:14:45,440 --> 00:14:46,519
This is marijuana.

279
00:14:46,639 --> 00:14:47,799
Have you tried it before?

280
00:15:04,480 --> 00:15:05,120
I'm so dizzy.

281
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:06,480
Careful, careful.

282
00:15:08,840 --> 00:15:10,440
Washing your face might make you feel a bit better.

283
00:15:47,200 --> 00:15:47,799
What is it, brother?

284
00:15:48,480 --> 00:15:49,120
A letter for you.

285
00:15:50,279 --> 00:15:51,240
It's from the school.

286
00:15:52,039 --> 00:15:52,519
Thanks, brother.

287
00:16:32,600 --> 00:16:33,120
Bro,

288
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,360
you mentioned having embassy connections.

289
00:16:36,679 --> 00:16:37,399
What kind of connections?

290
00:16:39,159 --> 00:16:40,240
What kind do you need?

291
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:44,919
It's from my school.

292
00:16:45,159 --> 00:16:46,360
I failed several classes,

293
00:16:46,519 --> 00:16:47,399
and they're telling me to drop out.

294
00:16:47,840 --> 00:16:49,000
I thought I could retake the exams.

295
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:51,679
This damn school's policies always change.

296
00:16:51,679 --> 00:16:53,080
Last year, you could still repeat the year.

297
00:16:53,159 --> 00:16:55,159
Bro, I can't drop out.

298
00:16:55,159 --> 00:16:56,480
If my family finds out about this,

299
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:57,639
they'll definitely go crazy.

300
00:16:58,000 --> 00:16:59,559
I can give it a try.

301
00:17:01,399 --> 00:17:03,039
But what can you offer them?

302
00:17:10,920 --> 00:17:12,359
Money? How much?

303
00:17:13,759 --> 00:17:15,599
They don't need a single dime.

304
00:17:15,960 --> 00:17:17,480
They just want to do business.

305
00:17:17,839 --> 00:17:19,200
What I mentioned last time...

306
00:17:19,519 --> 00:17:20,920
they want to see it too.

307
00:17:21,640 --> 00:17:23,440
Government economic documents.

308
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:24,440
Internal ones.

309
00:18:22,759 --> 00:18:23,519
Xiamen Eighth Market.

310
00:18:23,960 --> 00:18:25,000
Take it to Stall Six.

311
00:18:27,319 --> 00:18:28,599
Be careful not to drop it.

312
00:19:02,319 --> 00:19:03,000
Everyone, listen up!

313
00:19:03,240 --> 00:19:04,640
With the fishing ban these past few days,

314
00:19:05,079 --> 00:19:07,240
I brought you some seafood from Xiamen.

315
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:08,440
Fresh and top-notch!

316
00:19:08,440 --> 00:19:10,400
Take a look and pick what you want.

317
00:19:11,599 --> 00:19:12,319
Welcome, boss!

318
00:19:12,319 --> 00:19:13,480
I've got your goods ready.

319
00:19:18,440 --> 00:19:19,920
Feel free to take your pick.

320
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,000
Take whichever you like.

321
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:24,039
Have a look at this. Anything you want.

322
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:25,079
Take your pick, help yourself.

323
00:19:45,079 --> 00:19:45,960
I'm back.

324
00:19:46,240 --> 00:19:46,960
You're back.

325
00:19:51,759 --> 00:19:52,400
Come here.

326
00:19:59,519 --> 00:20:00,319
What's this?

327
00:20:00,720 --> 00:20:01,640
Cell phones.

328
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:02,680
Smuggled ones.

329
00:20:04,799 --> 00:20:06,119
New stuff from the Americans.

330
00:20:06,319 --> 00:20:07,599
The first one is a phone cloner.

331
00:20:07,599 --> 00:20:09,000
It looks a bit like a brick phone.

332
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:11,119
It intercepts nearby phone numbers,

333
00:20:11,119 --> 00:20:12,039
impersonates them,

334
00:20:12,039 --> 00:20:12,839
and puts them to our use.

335
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Over on the mainland,

336
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,839
we won't need fake SIM cards anymore,

337
00:20:15,839 --> 00:20:16,599
leaving no trace behind.

338
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,240
This is the Pacific Nightclub's

339
00:20:20,240 --> 00:20:21,440
legal representative,

340
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:23,759
but the actual controller is Wen Zongshu.

341
00:20:23,759 --> 00:20:25,440
Anyone who knows Boss Wen knows

342
00:20:25,440 --> 00:20:26,279
he doesn't mind taking a loss

343
00:20:26,279 --> 00:20:27,160
and spends generously.

344
00:20:27,359 --> 00:20:29,599
His car always has good smokes and drinks,

345
00:20:29,599 --> 00:20:31,400
he always carries plenty of cash,

346
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:33,839
always paying bills or bringing gifts.

347
00:20:33,839 --> 00:20:34,839
He's humble and polite,

348
00:20:34,839 --> 00:20:36,480
drains his glass with anyone,

349
00:20:36,480 --> 00:20:38,359
whether you're a driver or a superior.

350
00:20:38,359 --> 00:20:40,160
People from all walks of life praise him,

351
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:42,720
but in reality, he's deep in debt,

352
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:44,359
constantly robbing Peter to pay Paul.

353
00:20:44,359 --> 00:20:45,279
His family roots are in Quanzhou.

354
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:47,640
He went overseas with relatives as a kid,

355
00:20:47,640 --> 00:20:48,480
went to Hong Kong, China,

356
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:49,279
went to Macau, China,

357
00:20:49,279 --> 00:20:50,359
and also Southeast Asia,

358
00:20:50,359 --> 00:20:51,599
but never made it.

359
00:20:51,599 --> 00:20:52,480
Eventually, he went to Europe,

360
00:20:52,480 --> 00:20:53,319
took dangerous risks,

361
00:20:53,319 --> 00:20:54,799
made his first pot of gold,

362
00:20:55,000 --> 00:20:56,440
and opened an overseas travel agency.

363
00:20:56,440 --> 00:20:58,000
Later, he went to Taiwan, China,

364
00:20:58,240 --> 00:20:59,440
contracted a hotel,

365
00:20:59,440 --> 00:21:00,920
and grew his business step by step.

366
00:21:01,079 --> 00:21:03,319
Rumor says he committed murder in Taiwan, China,

367
00:21:03,319 --> 00:21:04,680
and was put on a police border watchlist.

368
00:21:04,680 --> 00:21:06,480
If not for help from the MIB,

369
00:21:06,839 --> 00:21:08,119
he never would've gotten out.

370
00:21:08,400 --> 00:21:09,039
After that,

371
00:21:09,039 --> 00:21:10,079
he returned to the mainland

372
00:21:10,079 --> 00:21:10,920
to clean up his identity.

373
00:21:11,160 --> 00:21:13,400
Now he's the vice president

374
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,240
and secretary of the City Calligraphy Association.

375
00:21:14,559 --> 00:21:15,440
He'll do any job,

376
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:16,599
helps anyone out,

377
00:21:16,599 --> 00:21:18,039
and has ties on both sides of the law.

378
00:21:18,039 --> 00:21:19,640
Years ago, he ran underground banks

379
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,039
and forged fake identities.

380
00:21:21,039 --> 00:21:22,839
We traced his funding sources,

381
00:21:22,839 --> 00:21:24,839
and they're mostly overseas accounts.

382
00:21:24,839 --> 00:21:26,000
He also travels abroad regularly,

383
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,359
under the pretext of doing business,

384
00:21:27,359 --> 00:21:29,119
to collect funds from Taiwan, China's MIB.

385
00:21:29,359 --> 00:21:30,640
As for this legal representative,

386
00:21:30,839 --> 00:21:33,359
her registered name is Liu Shangju.

387
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:34,319
In a nightclub,

388
00:21:34,319 --> 00:21:35,680
everyone uses an alias.

389
00:21:35,680 --> 00:21:36,960
Everyone calls her Sister Xia,

390
00:21:36,960 --> 00:21:38,279
or Xia Meimei if pushed further.

391
00:21:38,680 --> 00:21:40,480
When did she get with Wen Zongshu?

392
00:21:41,759 --> 00:21:42,640
Way back.

393
00:21:42,640 --> 00:21:44,200
No one expected them to end up together.

394
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:45,319
In the nightlife scene,

395
00:21:45,319 --> 00:21:46,599
it's all just one-night fun.

396
00:21:46,599 --> 00:21:47,880
Wen Zongshu has tasted plenty

397
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:48,759
and seen plenty.

398
00:21:48,759 --> 00:21:50,079
How could he truly love her?

399
00:21:50,319 --> 00:21:52,599
She looks sharp and capable,

400
00:21:52,759 --> 00:21:53,839
and crucially, she's reliable.

401
00:21:54,119 --> 00:21:55,839
She handles even the smallest tasks well,

402
00:21:55,839 --> 00:21:57,680
meticulous, loyal, and true to her word.

403
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:58,839
She's sharper than a lot of men.

404
00:21:59,079 --> 00:22:00,079
A woman like that

405
00:22:00,079 --> 00:22:01,680
is clearly the best choice for a courier.

406
00:22:02,119 --> 00:22:03,480
As long as we watch her closely,

407
00:22:03,480 --> 00:22:04,799
the leads will keep pouring in.

408
00:22:05,119 --> 00:22:07,880
Those tapes Cao Liaoping had

409
00:22:07,880 --> 00:22:09,480
were always kept in the lockers.

410
00:22:09,480 --> 00:22:10,400
He'd go in to sing,

411
00:22:10,799 --> 00:22:11,799
and by the time he came out,

412
00:22:11,799 --> 00:22:13,039
the tapes were still there,

413
00:22:13,039 --> 00:22:14,519
but they'd already been duplicated.

414
00:22:14,920 --> 00:22:16,200
Now that Cao Liaoping is compromised,

415
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:18,400
won't they pass intel somewhere else?

416
00:22:18,799 --> 00:22:20,279
If I were the MIB,

417
00:22:20,480 --> 00:22:22,279
and dared to use the Pacific again,

418
00:22:22,279 --> 00:22:24,519
I'd swap the drawer, not the desk,

419
00:22:24,759 --> 00:22:25,880
change the medicine, not the jar.

420
00:22:26,160 --> 00:22:27,279
There's no other place

421
00:22:27,279 --> 00:22:29,400
that gives them easier control.

422
00:22:29,400 --> 00:22:31,680
Using the same drop point twice in a row?

423
00:22:31,680 --> 00:22:32,480
An Empty Fort Strategy.

424
00:22:32,480 --> 00:22:33,279
They're gambling too.

425
00:22:33,799 --> 00:22:35,160
The lockers have been upgraded.

426
00:22:35,160 --> 00:22:36,599
Enter a passcode to open it.

427
00:22:36,599 --> 00:22:38,200
The handoff takes just a blink of an eye.

428
00:22:38,839 --> 00:22:40,039
Neither party needs to meet.

429
00:22:40,319 --> 00:22:41,480
A scene left behind, but zero evidence.

430
00:22:41,839 --> 00:22:42,920
We can't cut this thread.

431
00:22:43,279 --> 00:22:44,079
Let's keep the line baited.

432
00:22:44,359 --> 00:22:45,519
Intelligence shows

433
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,759
phone cloners from Taiwan, China

434
00:22:48,359 --> 00:22:49,599
has already arrived on the mainland.

435
00:22:49,839 --> 00:22:52,200
If their channel is also the Pacific,

436
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:55,119
that means it handles both people and cargo.

437
00:22:55,640 --> 00:22:57,240
We can probe into it as well.

438
00:22:59,920 --> 00:23:01,119
Play the long game to catch a big fish.

439
00:23:01,319 --> 00:23:02,839
What if Wen Zongshu catches on?

440
00:23:03,279 --> 00:23:04,039
Won't he run?

441
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:05,799
You deal with him all the time.

442
00:23:06,240 --> 00:23:07,200
You know him pretty well.

443
00:23:07,359 --> 00:23:09,359
How sharp do you think he is?

444
00:23:09,920 --> 00:23:10,880
Would he notice?

445
00:23:11,519 --> 00:23:12,720
It's not impossible.

446
00:23:13,319 --> 00:23:13,920
Right?

447
00:23:17,880 --> 00:23:19,519
Then you need to protect yourself.

448
00:23:19,519 --> 00:23:20,400
Don't blow your cover.

449
00:23:23,559 --> 00:23:24,720
Welcome.

450
00:24:22,839 --> 00:24:26,000
Good evening, boss.

451
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:20,960
What are you looking for?

452
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:34,720
Boss Wen,

453
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:36,279
let me light that for you.

454
00:26:06,279 --> 00:26:07,000
Brother Qi.

455
00:26:07,000 --> 00:26:07,799
You're here too.

456
00:26:08,400 --> 00:26:09,799
Come on over.

457
00:26:15,559 --> 00:26:16,440
Your old friend,

458
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:18,640
your best buddy Lin Kanshan is coming back.

459
00:26:19,039 --> 00:26:19,559
You heard, right?

460
00:26:20,160 --> 00:26:20,680
Yeah, I know.

461
00:26:20,839 --> 00:26:22,119
Word's been going around our circle.

462
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:24,240
He's expanding his factory,

463
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:26,039
and hosting a celebration soon.

464
00:26:26,359 --> 00:26:28,400
If you get an invitation, you should go.

465
00:26:28,680 --> 00:26:29,279
Brother Qi,

466
00:26:29,279 --> 00:26:30,119
stop joking around.

467
00:26:30,119 --> 00:26:30,960
If the two of us meet,

468
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:32,119
we'll definitely come to blows.

469
00:26:34,119 --> 00:26:34,759
Don't worry.

470
00:26:35,160 --> 00:26:35,799
With me around,

471
00:26:35,799 --> 00:26:37,119
he wouldn't dare touch a hair on your head.

472
00:26:38,599 --> 00:26:40,160
Better to make peace than hold a grudge.

473
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:42,079
Who says you two can't do business together?

474
00:26:42,359 --> 00:26:43,680
It beats going against each other.

475
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:44,680
Don't you think?

476
00:26:47,799 --> 00:26:48,440
Of course.

477
00:27:18,440 --> 00:27:19,920
You're three minutes late.

478
00:27:20,119 --> 00:27:21,119
In another 28 seconds,

479
00:27:21,720 --> 00:27:23,319
this meeting would've been canceled.

480
00:27:24,119 --> 00:27:25,160
I got stuck in traffic.

481
00:27:25,160 --> 00:27:26,599
Then you should've left earlier.

482
00:27:26,599 --> 00:27:27,599
I don't accept that excuse.

483
00:27:27,599 --> 00:27:29,079
I did leave early,

484
00:27:29,480 --> 00:27:30,480
but I didn't expect

485
00:27:30,759 --> 00:27:33,279
an accident around the bend ahead.

486
00:27:33,279 --> 00:27:34,000
Enough.

487
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:35,440
The point is, you're late.

488
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,599
What's the point of making excuses?

489
00:27:42,160 --> 00:27:43,240
On Wen Zongshu's end,

490
00:27:43,960 --> 00:27:45,519
anything unusual lately?

491
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:48,359
Nothing.

492
00:27:50,480 --> 00:27:51,400
Two weeks ago,

493
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:53,640
you gave me that exact answer.

494
00:27:55,519 --> 00:27:57,039
I can't get too close to him.

495
00:27:57,039 --> 00:27:58,000
Can't get too close?

496
00:27:58,000 --> 00:27:58,680
What about from now on?

497
00:27:59,240 --> 00:28:00,920
Are you always going to stay this far?

498
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:01,400
I...

499
00:28:03,359 --> 00:28:04,039
Give it to me straight.

500
00:28:04,440 --> 00:28:06,279
When can you find something new?

501
00:28:10,319 --> 00:28:11,200
To me,

502
00:28:12,160 --> 00:28:14,720
attitude matters far more than ability.

503
00:28:15,559 --> 00:28:17,519
Don't keep me waiting too long.

504
00:28:23,279 --> 00:28:24,599
I told you before

505
00:28:25,079 --> 00:28:26,640
not to talk over the phone.

506
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:28,599
That's why I didn't answer your call the other day.

507
00:28:28,599 --> 00:28:29,559
What is it?

508
00:28:31,039 --> 00:28:32,680
I graduated years ago,

509
00:28:32,960 --> 00:28:34,240
and still haven't settled my registration.

510
00:28:34,799 --> 00:28:35,960
I don't have an employer.

511
00:28:37,640 --> 00:28:39,359
Otherwise, I'll have to go back to Sichuan.

512
00:28:40,359 --> 00:28:41,480
Could you please...

513
00:28:42,559 --> 00:28:44,960
find a way to help me?

514
00:28:45,519 --> 00:28:46,759
What about your school?

515
00:28:46,759 --> 00:28:48,440
Why can't you get collective registration?

516
00:28:50,079 --> 00:28:51,000
Just because

517
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,400
that dean of yours

518
00:28:52,400 --> 00:28:54,480
ran into you at a nightclub?

519
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:58,920
What's that supposed to be?

520
00:28:58,920 --> 00:28:59,720
A disciplinary sanction?

521
00:29:01,519 --> 00:29:03,200
So what's the school saying now?

522
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,039
Forget it.

523
00:29:53,680 --> 00:29:55,599
Didn't you say you'd return at year-end?

524
00:29:56,400 --> 00:29:58,440
Could you go pick something up for me?

525
00:30:42,359 --> 00:30:43,599
Taiwan, China.

526
00:30:44,920 --> 00:30:50,440
52019740727.

527
00:30:55,799 --> 00:30:57,759
Which digit was I on just now?

528
00:30:58,400 --> 00:30:59,359
Forget it, forget it.

529
00:31:00,119 --> 00:31:01,480
You take over in a bit.

530
00:31:01,720 --> 00:31:03,680
Numbers are giving me a headache lately.

531
00:31:04,000 --> 00:31:05,119
A real headache, seriously.

532
00:31:05,200 --> 00:31:06,000
I don't know if

533
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:08,279
I left the window open last night,

534
00:31:09,119 --> 00:31:10,240
and caught a cold from the draft.

535
00:31:12,039 --> 00:31:13,839
You volunteer when you're not needed,

536
00:31:14,359 --> 00:31:15,960
and get a headache after guessing for 3 days.

537
00:31:16,559 --> 00:31:18,079
Who knows if you're really sick or faking it.

538
00:31:18,240 --> 00:31:19,720
How are you any different from Lin Kanshan?

539
00:31:20,200 --> 00:31:21,160
Lin Kanshan?

540
00:31:21,440 --> 00:31:22,039
Yeah.

541
00:31:22,519 --> 00:31:23,640
Jin Lina,

542
00:31:23,759 --> 00:31:24,720
Qian Wenying...

543
00:31:24,920 --> 00:31:26,480
He goes after women right around him,

544
00:31:26,480 --> 00:31:27,480
and runs off once he's seduced them.

545
00:31:28,119 --> 00:31:28,839
Isn't that right?

546
00:31:29,279 --> 00:31:31,720
Boss Lin would probably never imagine

547
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:33,839
that those who know him best in the world

548
00:31:34,160 --> 00:31:35,160
aren't his parents,

549
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:36,319
nor his colleagues,

550
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:39,440
but two neighbors who met purely by chance.

551
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:41,359
That's what long-term surveillance does.

552
00:31:42,119 --> 00:31:44,200
You get incredibly familiar with his voice,

553
00:31:44,200 --> 00:31:45,799
their habits, and their personality.

554
00:31:46,319 --> 00:31:47,400
Over time,

555
00:31:48,839 --> 00:31:50,799
your familiarity and understanding of him

556
00:31:51,440 --> 00:31:53,119
might even surpass his own.

557
00:31:53,519 --> 00:31:54,960
Whenever something happens,

558
00:31:55,279 --> 00:31:58,079
you know what he'll say

559
00:31:58,200 --> 00:31:59,119
and what he'll do.

560
00:31:59,680 --> 00:32:01,519
Yet however familiar you are with someone,

561
00:32:02,960 --> 00:32:04,640
do you truly understand him?

562
00:32:18,440 --> 00:32:21,079
Are you talking about me, or someone else?

563
00:32:23,440 --> 00:32:25,720
Your headache isn't from the draft.

564
00:32:26,680 --> 00:32:27,640
It's because of him.

565
00:32:34,440 --> 00:32:37,680
If you suspect someone or something,

566
00:32:38,640 --> 00:32:40,240
something you can see but can't touch,

567
00:32:40,559 --> 00:32:41,400
what would you do?

568
00:32:43,160 --> 00:32:44,680
If I suspected you,

569
00:32:45,039 --> 00:32:46,519
as long as you're alive,

570
00:32:46,799 --> 00:32:47,920
and as long as I'm alive,

571
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:49,720
I'd keep tailing you.

572
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:51,720
All the way to the nursing home,

573
00:32:52,079 --> 00:32:53,079
all the way to the grave.

574
00:33:18,039 --> 00:33:19,279
Lin Kanshan!

575
00:33:26,680 --> 00:33:27,839
Boss Lin!

576
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:29,920
Long time no see!

577
00:33:31,839 --> 00:33:32,400
Where's Brother Xiao?

578
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:32,960
He's not here.

579
00:33:33,839 --> 00:33:34,559
Boss Lin,

580
00:33:34,559 --> 00:33:35,079
come on in.

581
00:33:35,079 --> 00:33:36,000
Did you miss me?

582
00:33:36,359 --> 00:33:37,480
Missed you like crazy!

583
00:33:39,880 --> 00:33:41,799
You haven't changed much at all.

584
00:33:42,200 --> 00:33:43,519
Gone for so many years.

585
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:45,519
We were just betting last week

586
00:33:45,519 --> 00:33:46,880
that you'd definitely never come back.

587
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:47,920
You didn't even call me,

588
00:33:47,920 --> 00:33:49,279
nor visit me in Taiwan, China.

589
00:33:49,279 --> 00:33:50,240
You definitely didn't miss me.

590
00:33:50,440 --> 00:33:51,799
What do you mean I didn't miss you?

591
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:55,039
Wherever the meat is, that's where you go.

592
00:33:55,039 --> 00:33:56,680
You're the shrewdest of all.

593
00:33:56,680 --> 00:33:57,400
You found out Computed Tomography scanner

594
00:33:57,400 --> 00:33:58,440
leasing was profitable,

595
00:33:58,440 --> 00:34:00,400
and dumped us to hoard all the profits.

596
00:34:01,480 --> 00:34:02,200
Let me ask you:

597
00:34:02,319 --> 00:34:04,240
right now in Jiangxi and Guangdong,

598
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:05,880
don't you have the most machines?

599
00:34:06,279 --> 00:34:09,360
Brother Xiao, three monks get no water.

600
00:34:09,559 --> 00:34:10,480
If I take an extra bite,

601
00:34:10,480 --> 00:34:12,119
that's one less bite for you and Brother Qi.

602
00:34:12,119 --> 00:34:13,719
Wasn't I just looking out for my brothers?

603
00:34:13,719 --> 00:34:14,519
Just kidding.

604
00:34:14,920 --> 00:34:16,639
Is your place next door still there?

605
00:34:16,639 --> 00:34:17,920
Did you buy it?

606
00:34:18,440 --> 00:34:20,360
If you've got money, definitely buy property.

607
00:34:20,360 --> 00:34:21,400
Sister Lan, take my advice.

608
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:23,480
Prime downtown spots are a no-brainer.

609
00:34:23,480 --> 00:34:24,360
Just buy with your eyes closed.

610
00:34:24,360 --> 00:34:25,679
Prices are bound to skyrocket later.

611
00:34:25,679 --> 00:34:26,639
That landlord of mine

612
00:34:26,639 --> 00:34:28,000
moved abroad and isn't coming back.

613
00:34:28,280 --> 00:34:30,519
Renting long-term can't beat buying.

614
00:34:30,519 --> 00:34:33,199
I did come back for the property deed,

615
00:34:33,400 --> 00:34:35,119
but I always arrived in the dead of night

616
00:34:35,119 --> 00:34:36,239
and left at the crack of dawn.

617
00:34:36,239 --> 00:34:37,880
I didn't have time to visit you guys.

618
00:34:38,199 --> 00:34:39,639
No wonder Boss Lin struck it rich.

619
00:34:39,639 --> 00:34:41,679
Turns out you were running covert operations.

620
00:34:42,079 --> 00:34:43,400
Making a quiet fortune, eh?

621
00:34:45,039 --> 00:34:46,239
So how much did you buy it for?

622
00:34:46,519 --> 00:34:48,360
A second-hand house, was it dirt cheap?

623
00:34:49,480 --> 00:34:51,519
Chinese people love buying houses and land.

624
00:34:51,519 --> 00:34:52,920
As long as you have money in hand,

625
00:34:52,920 --> 00:34:54,639
housing prices will just keep climbing.

626
00:34:54,639 --> 00:34:56,559
Just look at Hong Kong, China and Taiwan, China.

627
00:34:57,280 --> 00:34:59,719
Boss Lin, are you back visiting family,

628
00:34:59,719 --> 00:35:00,559
or staying for good?

629
00:35:00,800 --> 00:35:01,559
Will you be leaving again?

630
00:35:02,840 --> 00:35:05,159
Do you want me to stay, or to leave?

631
00:35:07,079 --> 00:35:08,400
If you leave, we talk one way;

632
00:35:08,880 --> 00:35:09,880
if you stay, we talk another way.

633
00:35:11,039 --> 00:35:11,679
What do you mean?

634
00:35:12,639 --> 00:35:15,400
I don't know about Jiangxi and Guangdong,

635
00:35:15,400 --> 00:35:16,679
but our leasing business

636
00:35:16,679 --> 00:35:18,039
is almost at an end.

637
00:35:18,039 --> 00:35:18,800
After reform and opening up,

638
00:35:18,800 --> 00:35:20,440
hospitals have money now.

639
00:35:20,440 --> 00:35:22,159
Who still buys second-hand, obsolete junk?

640
00:35:22,159 --> 00:35:23,679
Everyone buys brand-new now.

641
00:35:23,679 --> 00:35:26,280
We've switched to medical equipment sales.

642
00:35:26,280 --> 00:35:27,639
You're still doing that?

643
00:35:28,480 --> 00:35:30,159
Everyone's doing real estate nowadays.

644
00:35:30,159 --> 00:35:32,960
What we're doing is just like real estate.

645
00:35:32,960 --> 00:35:34,840
It's just property and property management.

646
00:35:34,840 --> 00:35:36,679
Selling our equipment is only step one.

647
00:35:36,679 --> 00:35:38,320
Contracting maintenance is step two.

648
00:35:38,320 --> 00:35:39,880
First we sell our products,

649
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,440
then we sell our maintenance services.

650
00:35:41,440 --> 00:35:42,639
A steady stream of revenue—

651
00:35:42,639 --> 00:35:43,800
it'll feed us for at least ten years.

652
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:45,159
The only drawback

653
00:35:45,159 --> 00:35:46,840
is that the funding gap is quite large.

654
00:35:47,159 --> 00:35:47,880
I wonder if Boss Lin

655
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:49,239
would be interested in teaming up?

656
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:50,840
No problem.

657
00:35:51,079 --> 00:35:52,559
Don't worry about the funding,

658
00:35:52,679 --> 00:35:53,639
I'll take care of it.

659
00:35:54,519 --> 00:35:55,719
Parted for three days,

660
00:35:55,719 --> 00:35:57,280
and one sees you in a whole new light.

661
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:59,639
Boss Lin is getting richer and bolder by the day.

662
00:36:01,440 --> 00:36:02,199
Where's your big brother?

663
00:36:02,760 --> 00:36:03,800
Where is Brother Qi?

664
00:36:09,599 --> 00:36:11,119
Aren't you two working together anymore?

665
00:36:11,639 --> 00:36:13,199
Are you keeping all the profits to yourself too?

666
00:36:13,199 --> 00:36:14,159
No, no.

667
00:36:14,159 --> 00:36:15,000
We're still together.

668
00:36:15,119 --> 00:36:15,960
Still working together.

669
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:17,920
Give him a call.

670
00:36:30,320 --> 00:36:31,559
I'll give you two chances.

671
00:36:32,679 --> 00:36:33,760
Guess who I am.

672
00:36:37,840 --> 00:36:38,880
Boss Lin.

673
00:36:40,199 --> 00:36:41,000
Brother Qi.

674
00:36:41,400 --> 00:36:41,960
Those ears of yours...

675
00:36:41,960 --> 00:36:43,840
are truly sharper than a hound's.

676
00:36:44,719 --> 00:36:47,559
I'm with Chunxiao and Jinlan right now.

677
00:36:50,039 --> 00:36:50,639
Yeah.

678
00:36:50,639 --> 00:36:51,639
I'm back.

679
00:36:52,199 --> 00:36:53,400
Of course.

680
00:36:53,400 --> 00:36:54,039
The three of us...

681
00:36:54,039 --> 00:36:55,639
will be doing business together again.

682
00:36:55,639 --> 00:36:56,920
We bring each other good fortune, after all.

683
00:36:59,960 --> 00:37:01,840
Now that I'm back, we won't split up.

684
00:37:29,840 --> 00:37:30,480
Thanks.

685
00:37:46,800 --> 00:37:47,719
A cup of sugarcane juice,

686
00:37:48,639 --> 00:37:49,400
diluted with a bit of water.

687
00:38:17,239 --> 00:38:19,079
Lin Kanshan is back.

688
00:38:21,360 --> 00:38:22,800
Lina is with him.

689
00:38:24,440 --> 00:38:25,400
Right now.

690
00:38:57,840 --> 00:38:59,519
Lin Kanshan is finally back.

691
00:39:01,360 --> 00:39:02,320
All these years,

692
00:39:03,480 --> 00:39:04,679
we didn't wait in vain.

693
00:39:07,320 --> 00:39:08,119
What's he doing?

694
00:39:11,199 --> 00:39:11,960
Take a guess.

695
00:39:13,280 --> 00:39:14,400
How am I supposed to guess?

696
00:39:16,159 --> 00:39:17,000
What's wrong?

697
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:20,159
Listen for yourself.

698
00:39:51,079 --> 00:39:51,960
Now?

699
00:39:52,880 --> 00:39:55,280
Does my mouth still feel like Play-Doh?

700
00:39:59,119 --> 00:40:00,159
Not for a while now.

701
00:40:02,239 --> 00:40:03,719
More like a scented eraser.

702
00:40:18,440 --> 00:40:21,039
I am the last passerby on your road,

703
00:40:22,599 --> 00:40:24,159
the last spring,

704
00:40:24,800 --> 00:40:26,280
the last snow,

705
00:40:27,559 --> 00:40:30,000
the last battle for survival.

706
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:32,400
The night's swallowable sorrow

707
00:40:32,639 --> 00:40:34,119
has burst into flames,

708
00:40:34,760 --> 00:40:38,400
and ashes turn into joyful, lovely flowers.

709
00:40:40,039 --> 00:40:40,840
Did you write that?

710
00:40:42,679 --> 00:40:43,519
Just copied it.

711
00:40:46,480 --> 00:40:48,440
How could I write such a good poem?

712
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:50,960
What's the poem called?

713
00:40:51,440 --> 00:40:52,440
What does it mean?

714
00:40:54,920 --> 00:40:55,840
"Phoenix."

715
00:40:56,519 --> 00:40:58,360
It's by a 19-year-old poet,

716
00:40:58,360 --> 00:40:59,719
a poem written for his goddess.

717
00:41:00,599 --> 00:41:01,440
As for poetry,

718
00:41:02,199 --> 00:41:03,679
whatever you think it means,

719
00:41:04,239 --> 00:41:05,559
that's what it means.

720
00:41:07,719 --> 00:41:10,239
I never knew you liked this kind of stuff.

721
00:41:11,280 --> 00:41:13,639
I noticed your name on QQ is

722
00:41:13,639 --> 00:41:15,119
"Autumn."

723
00:41:15,119 --> 00:41:15,960
It's my pen name.

724
00:41:17,599 --> 00:41:20,280
The first time I published a poem in a magazine,

725
00:41:20,280 --> 00:41:21,599
that's the pen name I used.

726
00:41:23,679 --> 00:41:24,880
I like autumn.

727
00:41:28,199 --> 00:41:30,159
Fallen leaves everywhere.

728
00:41:30,559 --> 00:41:31,679
What's so good about that?

729
00:41:33,159 --> 00:41:34,840
It's just a bit cooler.

730
00:41:39,239 --> 00:41:40,440
I've heard

731
00:41:41,760 --> 00:41:43,360
people who like autumn

732
00:41:44,079 --> 00:41:45,480
tend to be more melancholy.

733
00:41:48,679 --> 00:41:50,280
You aren't usually like that.

734
00:41:55,880 --> 00:41:56,840
Are you?

735
00:41:58,639 --> 00:42:00,400
Have things been rough these past few years?

736
00:42:08,440 --> 00:42:09,880
Is someone bullying you?

737
00:42:10,880 --> 00:42:13,079
And more than one person, right?

738
00:42:15,960 --> 00:42:17,280
Who else besides Xiao Lu?

739
00:42:20,639 --> 00:42:22,239
You seem a bit afraid of this person,

740
00:42:25,559 --> 00:42:26,119
aren't you?

741
00:42:28,119 --> 00:42:29,599
Your uncle isn't around here either.

742
00:42:29,960 --> 00:42:30,880
Just who is it?

743
00:42:39,559 --> 00:42:40,480
People keep saying

744
00:42:41,719 --> 00:42:42,719
a war is coming,

745
00:42:42,960 --> 00:42:44,719
but people in Taipei and over here

746
00:42:44,719 --> 00:42:46,519
still have to live their normal lives.

747
00:42:46,519 --> 00:42:47,719
They still have to carry on.

748
00:42:48,239 --> 00:42:50,159
So what if the sky falls?

749
00:42:50,639 --> 00:42:52,320
You can always tell me whatever's bothering you.

750
00:42:55,719 --> 00:42:56,440
Who is it?

751
00:43:00,440 --> 00:43:02,719
Is someone forcing you to do something?

752
00:43:08,480 --> 00:43:09,559
I'm Wang Kai,

753
00:43:09,559 --> 00:43:11,280
inviting you to watch the drama series

754
00:43:11,280 --> 00:43:12,119
*Confrontation*.

755
00:43:12,119 --> 00:43:13,079
Before, during, and after the meal,

756
00:43:13,079 --> 00:43:14,239
you washed your hands three times.

757
00:43:14,559 --> 00:43:15,559
Going to the restroom—

758
00:43:15,559 --> 00:43:17,519
are you tailing me or Boss Ding?

759
00:43:17,519 --> 00:43:18,960
Who is the bacteria on your hands?

760
00:43:19,280 --> 00:43:20,800
Intelligence came in from Minzhong.

761
00:43:20,800 --> 00:43:22,360
Mainland State Security's bulletin says

762
00:43:22,360 --> 00:43:24,480
A-bian wants a "referendum,"

763
00:43:24,480 --> 00:43:25,920
and the Americans are going to apply pressure.

764
00:43:25,920 --> 00:43:27,679
Municipal and provincial internal notices,

765
00:43:27,679 --> 00:43:29,559
in less than 24 hours,

766
00:43:29,559 --> 00:43:31,400
are already sitting on desks in Taipei.

767
00:43:31,400 --> 00:43:32,639
An intentional leak.

768
00:43:32,639 --> 00:43:34,639
You still suspect Ma Qi is compromised?

769
00:43:34,639 --> 00:43:35,880
If he has turned traitor,

770
00:43:36,599 --> 00:43:38,079
he'll definitely be the hardest to handle.
